"The patient underwent a robot-assisted radical prostatectomy with a pathological stage pT4, positive surgical margins, and invasion of the seminal vesicles, with lymphovascular invasion present but no lymph node metastasis documented. Preoperative PSA was 16.8. The surgical findings indicate a high-risk profile. The prognosis is influenced by the positive margins and seminal vesicle invasion. The absence of documented biopsy grade differences between the biopsy and prostatectomy specimen widens uncertainty regarding the tumor characteristics. Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up information prevents a definitive assessment of the subsequent trajectory. The current heuristic horizon suggests a range for recurrence. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and its subsequent trajectory is crucial for revising this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 34.46 months. This is a predicted recurrence horizon, not evidence of observed recurrence. The sensitivity range is 25.85–43.08 months; its coverage has not been validated."
